  "question": "Let $X$ be the number of heads in 4 tosses of a fair coin. What is the probability that $X = 2$?",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "$n=4$, $p=0.5$.<br />$P(X=2)={4 \\choose 2}(0.5)^2(0.5)^2 = 6 \\times 0.25 \\times 0.25 = 6 \\times 0.0625 = 0.375 = \\frac{6}{16}$",
